Package: ensemblGraphQLr
Title: Modern Ensembl Queries via the Ensembl GraphQL API
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Marcelo", "Santos", , "XxMarce22@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A modern, high-performance successor to the 'biomaRt' package that
    retrieves Ensembl annotation through the Ensembl GraphQL API instead of the
    legacy BioMart and REST engines. Exposes a 'getBM()'-style user interface
    ('get_ensembl_data()') that maps biomaRt-style attribute and filter names
    onto a GraphQL query, executes it, and returns a flattened tibble. Network
    timeouts, dropped connections, server-side GraphQL errors and empty result
    sets are handled defensively, with empty typed tibbles returned whenever a
    query matches no records.
